      "name": "Berserk",
      "type": "feature",
      "img": "icons/magic/movement/abstract-ribbons-red-orange.webp",
      "system": {
        "active": true,
        "description": "<p>Whenever the clay golem starts its turn Bloodied, roll 1d6. On a 6, the clay golem goes berserk. On each of its turns while berserk, the clay golem attacks the nearest creature it can see. If no creature is near enough to move to and attack, the clay golem attacks an object. Once the clay golem goes berserk, it remains so until it is destroyed or it is no longer Bloodied.</p>",
        "ruleElements": []
      },
